<div class="non-normative">

*This technical report is non-normative.*

# Introduction # {#sctn-intro}

The [[native-app-payment-handler]] API defines an abstract functional model,
the [=native payment app provider model=], through which user agents can
interact with [=native payment apps=] in order to treat them as [=native-app
payment handlers=] that are accessible via the [[payment-request]] API.

This document describes one concrete implementation of that model, the
[=Android payment app provider=], which defines how a user agent running on the
Android Operating System can interact with other applications on the same
device that want to act as payment apps.

# Android Payment App Provider # {#sctn-android-payment-app-provider}

The <dfn>Android Payment App Provider</dfn> is a [=native payment app
provider=] that defines how a user agent can access Android [=native payment
apps=]. The necessary functionality is built on top of standard Android OS
concepts for cross-application communication and collaboration:

- <a href="https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/manifest/manifest-intro">AndroidManifest.xml</a>
- <a href="https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/intents/intents-filters">Intents</a>
- <a href="https://developer.android.com/develop/background-work/services">Services</a>

## Payment app AndroidManifest.xml ## {#sctn-payment-app-android-manifest}

In order to be visible to the user agent, the Android payment app defines the
following concepts in their `AndroidManifest.xml` file:

- A **mandatory** `PAY` Android activity, which will receive an intent when
    the user agent [=invokes the native payment app=].

- An **optional** `IS_READY_TO_PAY` Android service, which the user agent will
    bind to and call when determining if the app is [=able to handle a
    payment request=].

- An **optional** `UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS` Android service, which the user
    agent will bind to when communicating dynamic updates with the invoked
    [=native payment app=].

If an Android payment app specifies more than one activity or service that
matches one of the above, the user agent behavior is undefined.

### The `PAY` activity ### {#sctn-pay-activity}

The `PAY` activity will receive an intent from the user agent when the user
agent [=invokes the native payment app=] to handle a {{PaymentRequest}}. It
must be <a
href="https://developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/risks/android-exported">exported</a>
and have:

- An intent filter with an `org.chromium.intent.action.PAY` action
- An "`org.chromium.default_payment_method_name`" `<meta-data>` tag.
- Optionally, an "`org.chromium.payment_method_names`" `<meta-data>` tag.
- Optionally, an "`org.chromium.payment_supported_delegations`" `<meta-data>` tag.

The "`org.chromium.default_payment_method_name`" tag must have an
`android:value` attribute containing a valid [=url-based payment method
identifier=]. This will be used for determining the [=claimed payment method
identifier=].

The "`org.chromium.payment_method_names`" tag, if present, must have an
`android:resource` attribute pointing at a `<string-array>` resource each of
which must be a valid [=url-based payment method identifier=]. This will be
used for determining the [=claimed third-party origins=].

The "`org.chromium.payment_supported_delegations`" tag, if present, must have
an `android:resource` attribute pointing at a `<string-array>` resource listing
the [=supported delegations=] of the payment app.

<div class="example">
<xmp>
  <activity
       android:name=".PaymentActivity"
       android:exported="true">
    <intent-filter>
      <action android:name="org.chromium.intent.action.PAY" />
    </intent-filter>

    <meta-data
        android:name="org.chromium.default_payment_method_name"
        android:value="https://sampleapp.example/pay" />
    <meta-data
        android:name="org.chromium.payment_method_names"
        android:resource="@array/other_payment_method_names" />
    <meta-data
        android:name="org.chromium.payment_supported_delegations"
        android:resource="@array/supported_delegations" />
  </activity>
</xmp>
</div>

<div class="example">
<xmp>
  <resources>
    <string-array name="other_payment_method_names">
      <item>https://anotherapp.example/payment</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="supported_delegations">
      <item>shippingAddress</item>
      <item>payerName</item>
      <item>payerPhone</item>
      <item>payerEmail</item>
    </string-array>
  </resources>
</xmp>
</div>

ISSUE: The chromium.org namespace used here should be replaced by a w3.org one,
       but Chromium currently ships with chromium.org so it would need to be
       updated and a deprecation process followed, etc.

### The `IS_READY_TO_PAY` service ### {#sctn-is-ready-to-pay-service}

The `IS_READY_TO_PAY` service receives calls from the user agent to
determine if the app is [=able to handle a payment request=] (such as
checking whether the user has an enrolled payment instrument ready to pay). If
present, it must be <a
href="https://developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/risks/android-exported">exported</a>
and have an intent filter with an `org.chromium.intent.action.IS_READY_TO_PAY`
action.

<div class="example">
<xmp>
  <service
      android:name=".IsReadyToPayService"
      android:exported="true">
    <intent-filter>
      <action android:name="org.chromium.intent.action.IS_READY_TO_PAY" />
    </intent-filter>
  </service>
</xmp>
</div>

Communication with the service is defined by the following Android Interface
Definition Language (AIDL) interfaces:

<pre class="lang-java">
package org.chromium;

import org.chromium.IsReadyToPayServiceCallback;

// Implemented by the payment app.
interface IsReadyToPayService {
    oneway void isReadyToPay(
        IsReadyToPayServiceCallback callback, in Bundle parameters);
}
</pre>

<pre class="lang-java">
package org.chromium;

// Implemented by the user agent.
interface IsReadyToPayServiceCallback {
    oneway void handleIsReadyToPay(boolean isReadyToPay);
}
</pre>

ISSUE: As with the intent actions and meta-data tags, the `org.chromium` package
       namespace used by these AIDL interfaces should eventually be standardized
       under a vendor-neutral namespace such as `org.w3c.payments`.

The user agent calls the `isReadyToPay` method with a callback on which it
expects to receive the result of the readiness check, along with transaction
metadata in the `parameters` bundle (when checking if the app is [=able to
handle a payment request=]). The payment app then invokes `handleIsReadyToPay`
asynchronously when it is ready. This asynchronous flow ensures that an
unresponsive or slow payment application does not block or hang the user agent's
execution threads.

### The `UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS` service ### {#sctn-update-payment-details-service}

The `UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS` service receives connections from the user agent
when the payment app is invoked to facilitate two-way communication for
[[#sctn-dynamic-updates|dynamic updates]] (e.g. shipping address, shipping option,
or payment method changes). If present, it must be <a
href="https://developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/risks/android-exported">exported</a>
and have an intent filter with an
`org.chromium.intent.action.UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS` action.

<div class="example">
<xmp>
  <service
      android:name=".PaymentDetailsUpdateService"
      android:exported="true">
    <intent-filter>
      <action android:name="org.chromium.intent.action.UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS" />
    </intent-filter>
  </service>
</xmp>
</div>

Communication with the service is defined by the following Android Interface
Definition Language (AIDL) interfaces:

<pre class="lang-java">
package org.chromium.components.payments;

import android.os.Bundle;
import org.chromium.components.payments.IPaymentDetailsUpdateServiceCallback;

// Implemented by the user agent.
interface IPaymentDetailsUpdateService {
    oneway void changePaymentMethod(in Bundle paymentHandlerMethodData,
            IPaymentDetailsUpdateServiceCallback callback);
    oneway void changeShippingOption(in String shippingOptionId,
            IPaymentDetailsUpdateServiceCallback callback);
    oneway void changeShippingAddress(in Bundle shippingAddress,
            IPaymentDetailsUpdateServiceCallback callback);
}
</pre>

<pre class="lang-java">
package org.chromium.components.payments;

import android.os.Bundle;
import org.chromium.components.payments.IPaymentDetailsUpdateService;

// Implemented by the payment app.
interface IPaymentDetailsUpdateServiceCallback {
    oneway void updateWith(in Bundle updatedPaymentDetails);
    oneway void paymentDetailsNotUpdated();
    oneway void setPaymentDetailsUpdateService(
            IPaymentDetailsUpdateService service);
}
</pre>

ISSUE: As with the other intent actions and AIDL interfaces, the
       `org.chromium.components.payments` package namespace used here should
       eventually be standardized under a vendor-neutral namespace such as
       `org.w3c.payments`.

When the user agent [=invoke the native payment app|invokes=] the payment app's
`PAY` activity, it concurrently binds to the app's `UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS`
service (which implements `IPaymentDetailsUpdateServiceCallback`). Upon
connecting, the user agent calls `setPaymentDetailsUpdateService` to hand the
payment app a Binder proxy to the user agent's own
`IPaymentDetailsUpdateService` implementation.

When the user changes the payment method, shipping option, or shipping address
within the payment app UI, the payment app calls the corresponding method on
`IPaymentDetailsUpdateService`, passing the updated transaction parameters along
with a callback. The user agent then notifies the web merchant and, upon
receiving the merchant's response, communicates the updated payment details back
to the payment app via `updateWith` or `paymentDetailsNotUpdated`.

## User agent app AndroidManifest.xml ## {#sctn-user-agent-android-manifest}

In order to be able to interact with Android [=native payment apps=], the user
agent application <a
href="https://developer.android.com/training/package-visibility/declaring">declares
its package visibility needs</a> for the relevant intent filters in its own
AndroidManifest.xml file, by defining a `<queries>` block that lists the
following actions:

- `"org.chromium.intent.action.PAY"`
- `"org.chromium.intent.action.IS_READY_TO_PAY"`
- `"org.chromium.intent.action.UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS"`

<div class="example">
<xmp>
  <queries>
    <intent>
      <action android:name="org.chromium.intent.action.PAY"/>
    </intent>
    <intent>
      <action android:name="org.chromium.intent.action.IS_READY_TO_PAY"/>
    </intent>
    <intent>
      <action android:name="org.chromium.intent.action.UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS"/>
    </intent>
  </queries>
</xmp>
</div>

## Returning a list of native payment apps ## {#sctn-list-native-payment-apps}

In order to [=get the list of native payment apps=], the user agent performs
the following steps:

1. Create a new Intent object, |intent|, targeting the
     `org.chromium.intent.action.PAY` action.

1. Query the Android OS for the list of activities that can be performed for
     |intent|, for example via <a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/pm/PackageManager#queryIntentActivities(android.content.Intent,%20int)">PackageManager.queryIntentActivities</a>.

ISSUE: do we need to spec how to turn the resultant info into a list of
     apps? TBD.

## Claiming a method URL ## {#sctn-claiming-method-url}

The [=claimed payment method identifier=] for an Android application, |app|, is
the `android:value` attribute of the `org.chromium.default_payment_method_name`
`<meta-data>` tag in |app|'s AndroidManifest.xml file.

## Claiming a set of origins ## {#sctn-claiming-origins}

The [=set=] of [=claimed third-party origins=] for an Android application,
|app|, is created from the `org.chromium.payment_method_names` `<meta-data>`
tag in |app|'s AndroidManifest.xml file, as follows:

1. Let |paymentMethodIdentifiers| be the value  of the `org.chromium.payment_method_names`
    `<meta-data>` tag.

1. If |paymentMethodIdentifiers| is not a string array, return an empty [=set=].

1. Let |origins| be an empty [=set=].

1. For each string |identifier| in |paymentMethodIdentifiers|:

    1. If |identifier| is not a valid [=url-based payment method identifier=],
        go to the next iteration of the loop.

    1. Let |origin| be the [=origin=] of |identifier|.

    1. Add |origin| to |origins|.

1. Return |origins|.

ISSUE: We need to document why this is an array of method URLs, rather than
just an array of origins.

## Supported delegations ## {#sctn-supported-delegations}

The [=set=] of [=supported delegations=] for an Android application, |app|, is
created from the `org.chromium.payment_supported_delegations` `<meta-data>` tag
in |app|'s `PAY` activity, as follows:

1. Let |delegations| be an empty [=set=].

1. Let |delegationNames| be the string array resource referenced by the
     `org.chromium.payment_supported_delegations` `<meta-data>` tag in |app|'s
     `PAY` activity.

1. If |delegationNames| is null or empty, return |delegations|.

1. For each string |name| in |delegationNames|:

    1. If |name| is equal to `"shippingAddress"`, add
         {{PaymentDelegation/"shippingAddress"}} to |delegations|.

    1. Else if |name| is equal to `"payerName"`, add
         {{PaymentDelegation/"payerName"}} to |delegations|.

    1. Else if |name| is equal to `"payerPhone"`, add
         {{PaymentDelegation/"payerPhone"}} to |delegations|.

    1. Else if |name| is equal to `"payerEmail"`, add
         {{PaymentDelegation/"payerEmail"}} to |delegations|.

    1. Otherwise, ignore |name|.

1. Return |delegations|.

## Checking if a native payment app is a related application for a web app manifest ## {#sctn-checking-related-application}

In order to check if a given Android application, |app|, [=is a related
application=] for a [=application manifest|web app manifest=], |manifest|, the
user agent performs the following steps:

1. Let |packageName| be the package name of |app|.

1. Let |version| be the version of |app|.

1. Let |fingerprint| be ...

    ISSUE: TODO - need to specify how to convert it to a string

1. For each [=related application=], |relatedApplication|, in the [=related
     applications=] of |manifest|:

    1. If |packageName| is not equal to |relatedApplication|'s [=id=], go to
        the next iteration of this loop.

    1. If |version| is less than |relatedApplication|'s [=minimum version=],
        go to the next iteration of this loop.

        ISSUE: Need to define how the comparison is done.

    1. If |fingerprint| does not match |relatedApplication|'s [=fingerprint=],
        go to the next iteration of this loop.

    1. Return `true`.

1. Return `false`.

## Determining if an Android native payment app can handle a {{PaymentRequest}} ## {#sctn-hasenrolled-instrument}

In order to check if an Android application, |app|, is [=able to handle a
payment request=], |request|, the user agent performs the following steps:

1. If |app| does not have a service listed in its `AndroidManifest.xml` with an
     intent-filter for `org.chromium.intent.action.IS_READY_TO_PAY` (see
     [[#sctn-is-ready-to-pay-service]]), return `true`.

    NOTE: The `IS_READY_TO_PAY` service is optional. If a payment app does not
          provide it, the user agent assumes the app is ready and delegates
          the payment decision to when the app is invoked via the `PAY` activity.

1. Let |parameters| be a new Android Bundle object.

1. Insert the Android package name of the user agent application into
     |parameters| with the key `"packageName"`.

1. Let |topOrigin| be |request|'s [=relevant global object=]'s [=associated
     Document=]'s [=origin=], formatted without a scheme (e.g.
     `"merchant.example"`). Insert |topOrigin| into |parameters| with the key
     `"topLevelOrigin"`.

1. Let |iframeOrigin| be |request|'s [=relevant settings object=]'s [=environment
     settings object/origin=], formatted without a scheme. Insert |iframeOrigin|
     with the key `"paymentRequestOrigin"`.

1. If the top-level document was loaded over a secure HTTPS connection and a
     server certificate chain is available, let |certArray| be a Parcelable
     array containing each certificate's raw DER-encoded byte array inside an
     Android Bundle with key `"certificate"`. Insert |certArray| into
     |parameters| with the key `"topLevelCertificateChain"`.

1. Let |matchingMethodNames| be a new empty [=list=] of strings.

1. Let |methodDataBundle| be a new Android Bundle object.

1. For each [=payment method identifier=] |identifier| supported by |request|:

    1. If |app| [=is allowed to handle the payment method identifier=]
         |identifier|:

        1. Append |identifier| to |matchingMethodNames|.

        1. Let |dataString| be the JSON serialization of the method-specific
             data associated with |identifier| in |request|, or `"{}"` if no data
             was supplied.

        1. Insert |dataString| into |methodDataBundle| with key |identifier|.

1. Insert |matchingMethodNames| (as an ArrayList of strings) into |parameters|
     with the key `"methodNames"`.

1. Insert |methodDataBundle| into |parameters| with the key `"methodData"`.

1. Create a new Android Intent object targeting |app|'s package name, |app|'s
     `IS_READY_TO_PAY` service class name, and action
     `org.chromium.intent.action.IS_READY_TO_PAY`.

1. Bind to the service via <a
     href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/Context#bindService(android.content.Intent,%20android.content.ServiceConnection,%20int)">Context.bindService</a>
     using the `BIND_AUTO_CREATE` flag.

1. If binding fails or a user agent defined connection timeout expires before
     the service connects, unbind the service and return `false`.

1. On service connection, call `isReadyToPay(callback, parameters)` on the
     bound `IsReadyToPayService` interface.

     ISSUE: Providing the above parameters to the isReadyToPay call is a
     significant privacy issue. Websites and apps may collaborate to silently
     track the user using the various origins and custom method data included.
     While user agents can take steps to minimize this risk (e.g., requiring
     one-time user consent before allowing each (website, app) pair to connect,
     we should consider removing this information entirely from isReadyToPay.

1. Wait asynchronously for the `handleIsReadyToPay(isReadyToPay)` method to be
     invoked on the callback, subject to a user agent defined query timeout.

    1. If `handleIsReadyToPay` is called with boolean |isReadyToPay| before the
         timeout, unbind the service and return |isReadyToPay|.

    1. If the query times out, the service disconnects, or an exception occurs,
         unbind the service and return `false`.

## Invoking an Android native payment app ## {#sctn-invoking}

In order to [=invoke the native payment app=], |app|, for a {{PaymentRequest}}
|request|, the user agent performs the following steps:

1. Let |packageName| be the Android package name for |app|.
1. Let |activityName| be the Activity name for |app|.

     ISSUE: TODO - these name to be part of some sort of app concept

1. Let |extras| be the result of [=creating an Android bundle=] for |request|.

1. Create an Intent object, |intent|, whose:

    1. Class name is set to the combination of |packageName| and
         |activityName|, e.g. via <a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/Intent#setClassName(java.lang.String,%20java.lang.String)">Intent.setClassName</a>.

    1. Action is set to `org.chromium.intent.action.PAY`.

    1. Extras are set to |extras|, e.g. via
         <a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/Intent#putExtras(android.os.Bundle)">Intent.putExtras</a>.

1. If |app| declares an `UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS` service in its
     `AndroidManifest.xml`, [=establish the update service connection=]
     concurrently.

1. Send |intent| to the Android OS in such a way that the user agent will be
     notified on result, e.g. via <a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#startActivityForResult(android.content.Intent,%20int)">Activity.startActivityForResult</a>.

## Communicating with an invoked Android native payment app ## {#sctn-dynamic-updates}

An invoked [=native payment app=], |app|, can communicate dynamic transaction
changes (such as shipping address, shipping option, or payment method changes)
back to the web merchant via the `UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS` service (see
[[#sctn-update-payment-details-service]]).

### Establishing the update service connection ### {#sctn-dynamic-updates-connection}

The user agent performs the following steps to <dfn>establish the update service
connection</dfn> for an invoked [=native payment app=] |app|:

1. Create a new Android Intent object targeting |app|'s package name, |app|'s
     `UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS` service class name, and action
     `org.chromium.intent.action.UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS`.

1. Attempt to bind to the service via <a
     href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/Context#bindService(android.content.Intent,%20android.content.ServiceConnection,%20int)">Context.bindService</a>
     using the `BIND_AUTO_CREATE` flag.

     1. If binding fails, unbind the service and abort these steps.

          NOTE: The payment flow continues normally; the payment app will
                proceed without dynamic update capabilities.

1. When the service connection is established:

    1. Obtain the `IPaymentDetailsUpdateServiceCallback` interface from the
         returned IBinder.

    1. Call `setPaymentDetailsUpdateService` on that interface, passing the user
         agent's `IPaymentDetailsUpdateService` Binder instance.

1. Maintain this service connection active for the duration of the payment
     interaction. When |app|'s `PAY` activity finishes or is dismissed, unbind
     and terminate the service connection.

     1. If the connection is lost or dies unexpectedly while the payment
          interaction is still active, the user agent may attempt to reconnect.
          If the connection cannot be restored, the user agent unbinds the
          service and continues the payment flow without dynamic update
          capabilities.

### Authorizing service requests ### {#sctn-dynamic-updates-authorization}

To <dfn>authorize a dynamic update service request</dfn> from an application
|app|:

1. Let |callerUid| be the calling UID obtained via <a
     href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Binder#getCallingUid()">Binder.getCallingUid()</a>.

1. Query the Android OS for the package names and cryptographic signing
     certificates associated with |callerUid|.

1. If none of the packages matching |callerUid| have a package name equal to
     |app|'s package name, or if their signing certificates do not match |app|'s
     signing certificates, return `false`.

1. Return `true`.

### Handling payment method change ### {#sctn-dynamic-updates-method-change}

When `changePaymentMethod` is called on `IPaymentDetailsUpdateService` by
|app|, with `paymentHandlerMethodData` and `callback`:

1. If the user agent is unable to [=authorize a dynamic update service
     request=] from |app|, return.

1. If `paymentHandlerMethodData` is null, or if the string extra `"methodName"`
     in `paymentHandlerMethodData` is null or empty:

    1. Call `callback.updateWith` with a Bundle containing an error message, and
         return.

1. Let |methodName| be the string extra `"methodName"` in
     `paymentHandlerMethodData`.

1. Let |stringifiedDetails| be the string extra `"details"` in
     `paymentHandlerMethodData`, or `"{}"` if absent.

1. Let |methodDetails| be the result of parsing |stringifiedDetails| as a JSON
     object. If parsing throws an error, let |methodDetails| be null.

1. [=Inform the user agent that the user has changed their payment method=] with
     |app|, |methodName|, and |methodDetails|.

     ISSUE: Currently this algorithm only takes |methodDetails|. Taking |app|
            makes sense, but I believe the user agent should determine
            |methodName|.

### Handling shipping option change ### {#sctn-dynamic-updates-shipping-option-change}

When `changeShippingOption` is called on `IPaymentDetailsUpdateService` by
|app| with `shippingOptionId` and `callback`:

1. If the user agent is unable to [=authorize a dynamic update service
     request=] from |app|, return.

1. If `shippingOptionId` is null or empty:

    1. Call `callback.updateWith` with a Bundle containing an error message, and
         return.

1. [=Inform the user agent that the user has changed their shipping option=] with
     |app| and `shippingOptionId`.

     ISSUE: Currently this algorithm only takes `shippingOptionId`. Taking |app|
            makes sense, but we'll need to update spec.bs.

### Handling shipping address change ### {#sctn-dynamic-updates-shipping-address-change}

When `changeShippingAddress` is called on `IPaymentDetailsUpdateService` by
|app| with `shippingAddressBundle` and `callback`:

1. If the user agent is unable to [=authorize a dynamic update service
     request=] from |app|, return.

1. If `shippingAddressBundle` is null or empty:

    1. Call `callback.updateWith` with a Bundle containing an error message, and
         return.

1. Let |shippingAddress| be the result of [=parsing a shipping address Android
     bundle=] from `shippingAddressBundle`.

1. If |shippingAddress| is null:

    1. Call `callback.updateWith` with a Bundle containing an error message, and
         return.

1. [=Inform the user agent that the user has changed their shipping address=] with
     |app| and |shippingAddress|.

### Updating payment details ### {#sctn-dynamic-updates-update-details}

In order to [=update payment details=] for |app| with |detailsPromise|:

1. Upon fulfillment of |detailsPromise| with a {{PaymentRequestDetailsUpdate}}
     |update|:

    1. Let |bundle| be the result of [=creating an Android bundle from a
         PaymentRequestDetailsUpdate=] for |update|.

    1. Call `callback.updateWith(bundle)` on the active
         `IPaymentDetailsUpdateServiceCallback`.

1. Upon rejection of |detailsPromise|:

    1. Call `callback.paymentDetailsNotUpdated()` on the active
         `IPaymentDetailsUpdateServiceCallback`.

### Notifying payment details not updated ### {#sctn-dynamic-updates-not-updated}

In order to [=notify payment details not updated=] for |app|:

1. Call `callback.paymentDetailsNotUpdated()` on the active
     `IPaymentDetailsUpdateServiceCallback`.

### Parsing a shipping address Android bundle ### {#sctn-bundle-to-address}

To <dfn>parse a shipping address Android bundle</dfn> from an Android Bundle,
|bundle|:

1. Let |country| be the string extra `"countryCode"` in |bundle|.

1. If |country| is null, empty, or not a valid ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code,
     return null.

1. Let |address| be a new {{ContactAddress}} object with the following fields:

    - `country` set to |country|.
    - `addressLine` set to the string array extra `"addressLines"` in |bundle|,
        or an empty list if absent.
    - `region` set to the string extra `"region"` in |bundle|, or `""` if
        absent.
    - `city` set to the string extra `"city"` in |bundle|, or `""` if absent.
    - `dependentLocality` set to the string extra `"dependentLocality"` in
        |bundle|, or `""` if absent.
    - `postalCode` set to the string extra `"postalCode"` in |bundle|, or `""`
        if absent.
    - `sortingCode` set to the string extra `"sortingCode"` in |bundle|, or
        `""` if absent.
    - `organization` set to the string extra `"organization"` in |bundle|, or
        `""` if absent.
    - `recipient` set to the string extra `"recipient"` in |bundle|, or `""` if
        absent.
    - `phone` set to the string extra `"phone"` in |bundle|, or `""` if absent.

1. Return |address|.

### Creating an Android bundle from a PaymentRequestDetailsUpdate ### {#sctn-details-update-to-bundle}

To <dfn>create an Android bundle from a PaymentRequestDetailsUpdate</dfn> from
a {{PaymentRequestDetailsUpdate}}, |update|:

1. Let |bundle| be a new Android Bundle object.

1. If |update|["total"] exists:

    1. Let |totalBundle| be a new Android Bundle object containing:
        - `"currency"` set to |update|["total"]["amount"]["currency"]
        - `"value"` set to |update|["total"]["amount"]["value"]

    1. Insert |totalBundle| into |bundle| with key `"total"`.

1. If |update|["shippingOptions"] exists and is not empty:

    1. Let |optionsArray| be an empty Parcelable array.

    1. For each {{PaymentShippingOption}} |option| in |update|["shippingOptions"]:

        1. Let |optBundle| be a new Android Bundle object containing:
            - `"id"` set to |option|["id"]
            - `"label"` set to |option|["label"]
            - `"amount"` set to a Bundle containing `"currency"` and `"value"`
                from |option|["amount"]
            - `"selected"` set to |option|["selected"]

        1. Append |optBundle| to |optionsArray|.

    1. Insert |optionsArray| into |bundle| with key `"shippingOptions"`.

1. If |update|["error"] exists and is not empty:

    1. Insert |update|["error"] into |bundle| with key `"error"`.

1. If |update|["stringifiedPaymentMethodErrors"] exists and is not empty:

    1. Insert |update|["stringifiedPaymentMethodErrors"] into |bundle| with key
         `"stringifiedPaymentMethodErrors"`.

1. If |update|["shippingAddressErrors"] exists and is not null:

    1. Let |addrErrorsBundle| be a new Android Bundle object.

    1. For each key in |update|["shippingAddressErrors"] (such as `"country"`,
         `"addressLine"`, `"city"`, `"postalCode"`, etc.), insert the string
         error into |addrErrorsBundle| under that key.

    1. Insert |addrErrorsBundle| into |bundle| with key `"addressErrors"`.

1. Return |bundle|.

## Indicating success of an invoked Android native payment app ## {#sctn-indicate-success}

In order for an invoked Android application, |app|, to [=indicate success=]
back to the user agent, |app| performs the following steps:

1. Create a new Android Intent object, |intent|.

1. Insert the string identifier of the payment method selected by the user into
     |intent| with the key `"methodName"`.

1. Insert a JSON-stringified object containing the payment-method-specific
     transaction details into |intent| with the key `"details"`.

1. If |app| supports and was requested to provide payer information:

    1. If payer name collection was delegated, insert the payer's name string
         into |intent| with the key `"payerName"`.

    1. If payer email collection was delegated, insert the payer's email string
         into |intent| with the key `"payerEmail"`.

    1. If payer phone collection was delegated, insert the payer's phone string
         into |intent| with the key `"payerPhone"`.

1. If |app| supported and was requested to provide shipping information:

    1. Insert the identifier of the selected shipping option into |intent| with
         the key `"shippingOptionId"`.

    1. Let |addressBundle| be an Android Bundle representing the selected
         shipping address, populated with the address keys defined in
         [=parse a shipping address Android bundle=]. Insert |addressBundle|
         into |intent| with the key `"shippingAddress"`.

1. Call <a
     href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#setResult(int,%20android.content.Intent)">Activity.setResult</a>
     with <a
     href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#RESULT_OK">Activity.RESULT_OK</a>
     and |intent|.

1. Terminate |app|'s activity, e.g. via <a
     href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#finish()">Activity.finish()</a>.

To [=retrieve the converted result details=] from the payment activity's result
Intent, |resultIntent|, with the requested {{PaymentOptions}} |paymentOptions|,
the user agent performs the following steps:

1. If |resultIntent| is null or does not contain extras, return failure.

1. Let |extras| be the Bundle of extras from |resultIntent|.

1. Let |details| be the string extra `"details"` in |extras|.

1. If |details| is null or empty, return failure.

1. Let |methodName| be the string extra `"methodName"` in |extras|.

1. If |methodName| is null or empty, return failure.

1. Let |response| be a new {{NativePaymentHandlerResponse}} dictionary with:
    - |response|["methodName"] set to |methodName|
    - |response|["details"] set to |details|

1. If |paymentOptions| was supplied:

    1. If |paymentOptions|["requestShipping"] is true:

        1. Let |addressBundle| be the Bundle extra `"shippingAddress"` in |extras|.

        1. If |addressBundle| is null or empty, return failure.

        1. Let |shippingAddress| be the result of [=parsing a shipping address Android bundle=] from |addressBundle|.

        1. If |shippingAddress| is null, return failure.

        1. Set |response|["shippingAddress"] to |shippingAddress|.

        1. Let |shippingOptionId| be the string extra `"shippingOptionId"` in |extras|.

        1. If |shippingOptionId| is null or empty, return failure.

        1. Set |response|["shippingOption"] to |shippingOptionId|.

    1. If |paymentOptions|["requestPayerName"] is true:

        1. Let |payerName| be the string extra `"payerName"` in |extras|.

        1. If |payerName| is null or empty, return failure.

        1. Set |response|["payerName"] to |payerName|.

    1. If |paymentOptions|["requestPayerEmail"] is true:

        1. Let |payerEmail| be the string extra `"payerEmail"` in |extras|.

        1. If |payerEmail| is null or empty, return failure.

        1. Set |response|["payerEmail"] to |payerEmail|.

    1. If |paymentOptions|["requestPayerPhone"] is true:

        1. Let |payerPhone| be the string extra `"payerPhone"` in |extras|.

        1. If |payerPhone| is null or empty, return failure.

        1. Set |response|["payerPhone"] to |payerPhone|.

1. Return |response|.

## Indicating user cancel from an invoked Android native payment app ## {#sctn-indicate-user-cancel}

In order for an invoked Android application, |app|, to [=indicate user
cancellation=] back to the user agent, |app| performs the following steps:

1. Call <a
     href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#setResult(int)">Activity.setResult</a>
     with <a
     href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#RESULT_CANCEL">Activity.RESULT_CANCEL</a>.

1. Terminate |app|'s activity, e.g. via <a
     href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#finish()">Activity.finish()</a>.

## Indicating internal error from an invoked Android native payment app ## {#sctn-indicate-app-error}

In order for an invoked Android application, |app|, to [=indicate internal
error=] back to the user agent, |app| performs the following steps:

1. Let |RESULT_INTERNAL_ERROR| be equal to <a
     href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#RESULT_FIRST_USER">Activity.RESULT_FIRST_USER</a>
     (integer value `1`).

1. Call <a
     href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#setResult(int)">Activity.setResult</a>
     with |RESULT_INTERNAL_ERROR|.

1. Terminate |app|'s activity, e.g. via <a
     href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#finish()">Activity.finish()</a>.

## Creating an Android bundle ## {#sctn-creating-bundle}

To <dfn>create an Android bundle</dfn> from a {{PaymentRequest}}, |request|, for
an application |app|:

1. Let |bundle| be a new Android Bundle object.

1. Insert |request|.{{PaymentRequest/id}} into |bundle| with the key
     `"paymentRequestId"`.

1. Insert the {{Document/title}} of |request|'s [=relevant global object=]'s
     [=associated Document=] into |bundle| with the key `"merchantName"`.

1. Let |totalItem| be |request|.{{PaymentRequest/[[details]]}}.{{PaymentDetailsInit/total}}.

1. Let |serializedTotal| be a JSON-serialized object containing `"currency"` set
     to |totalItem|.{{PaymentItem/amount}}.{{PaymentCurrencyAmount/currency}}
     and `"value"` set to
     |totalItem|.{{PaymentItem/amount}}.{{PaymentCurrencyAmount/value}}. Insert
     |serializedTotal| into |bundle| with the key `"total"`.

1. If |request|.{{PaymentRequest/[[details]]}}.{{PaymentDetailsBase/modifiers}}
     exists and is not empty:

    1. Let |modifiersList| be an empty JSON array.

    1. For each {{PaymentDetailsModifier}} |modifier| in
         |request|.{{PaymentRequest/[[details]]}}.{{PaymentDetailsBase/modifiers}}:

        1. Let |modObj| be a new JSON object.

        1. If |modifier|.{{PaymentDetailsModifier/total}} exists, set
             |modObj|["total"] to a JSON object with `"currency"` and `"value"`
             from |modifier|.{{PaymentDetailsModifier/total}}.{{PaymentItem/amount}}.

        1. Set |modObj|["supportedMethods"] to a JSON array containing the
             single string |modifier|.{{PaymentDetailsModifier/supportedMethods}}.

        1. Set |modObj|["data"] to the JSON-serialized string of
             |modifier|.{{PaymentDetailsModifier/data}} if present, or `"{}"`
             otherwise.

        1. Append |modObj| to |modifiersList|.

    1. Insert the JSON-stringified serialization of |modifiersList| into
         |bundle| with the key `"modifiers"`.

1. Let |options| be |request|.{{PaymentRequest/[[options]]}}.

1. If |options| exists:

    1. Let |optionsBundle| be a new Android Bundle object containing:
        - `"requestPayerName"` set to |options|.{{PaymentOptions/requestPayerName}}
        - `"requestPayerEmail"` set to |options|.{{PaymentOptions/requestPayerEmail}}
        - `"requestPayerPhone"` set to |options|.{{PaymentOptions/requestPayerPhone}}
        - `"requestShipping"` set to |options|.{{PaymentOptions/requestShipping}}

    1. If |options|.{{PaymentOptions/shippingType}} exists and is not null:
        - Insert |options|.{{PaymentOptions/shippingType}} into |optionsBundle|
            with the key `"shippingType"`.

    1. Insert |optionsBundle| into |bundle| with the key `"paymentOptions"`.

1. If |options| exists and |options|.{{PaymentOptions/requestShipping}} is true:

    1. If |request|.{{PaymentRequest/[[details]]}}.{{PaymentDetailsBase/shippingOptions}}
         exists and is not empty:

        1. Let |optionsArray| be an empty Parcelable array.

        1. For each {{PaymentShippingOption}} |option| in
             |request|.{{PaymentRequest/[[details]]}}.{{PaymentDetailsBase/shippingOptions}}:

            1. Let |optBundle| be a new Android Bundle object containing:
                - `"id"` set to |option|.{{PaymentShippingOption/id}}
                - `"label"` set to |option|.{{PaymentShippingOption/label}}
                - `"amount"` set to a Bundle containing `"currency"` and
                    `"value"` from |option|.{{PaymentShippingOption/amount}}
                - `"selected"` set to |option|.{{PaymentShippingOption/selected}}

            1. Append |optBundle| to |optionsArray|.

        1. Insert |optionsArray| into |bundle| with the key `"shippingOptions"`.

1. Let |topOrigin| be |request|'s [=relevant global object=]'s [=associated
     Document=]'s [=origin=], formatted without a scheme (e.g.
     `"merchant.example"`). Insert |topOrigin| into |bundle| with the key
     `"topLevelOrigin"`.

1. Let |iframeOrigin| be |request|'s [=relevant settings object=]'s [=environment
     settings object/origin=], formatted without a scheme. Insert |iframeOrigin|
     into |bundle| with the key `"paymentRequestOrigin"`.

1. If the top-level document was loaded over a secure HTTPS connection and a
     server certificate chain is available, let |certArray| be a Parcelable
     array containing each certificate's raw DER-encoded byte array inside an
     Android Bundle with key `"certificate"`. Insert |certArray| into |bundle|
     with the key `"topLevelCertificateChain"`.

1. Let |matchingMethodNames| be a new empty [=list=] of strings.

1. Let |methodDataBundle| be a new Android Bundle object.

1. For each [=payment method identifier=] |identifier| supported by |request|:

    1. If |app| [=is allowed to handle the payment method identifier=]
         |identifier|:

        1. Append |identifier| to |matchingMethodNames|.

        1. Let |dataString| be the JSON serialization of the method-specific
             data associated with |identifier| in |request|, or `"{}"` if no data
             was supplied.

        1. Insert |dataString| into |methodDataBundle| with key |identifier|.

1. Insert |matchingMethodNames| (as an ArrayList of strings) into |bundle| with
     the key `"methodNames"`.

1. Insert |methodDataBundle| into |bundle| with the key `"methodData"`.

1. Return |bundle|.

</div>
